Description: Full Trinity Desktop Environment, curated (metapackage)
 A custom metapackage that installs a complete Trinity Desktop Environment
 (TDE) on Debian, built as an independent alternative to the stock
 tde-trinity, redmond-default-settings-trinity and
 redmond-default-settings-ii-trinity metapackages.
 .
 Compared to the stock metapackages, this package:
  - drops legacy/no-longer-needed components (kfloppy, k3b, cvs/cervisia
    and the rest of the tdesdk dev-tools module, lisa/kpf network
    discovery, tdebindings, and similar cruft)
  - does not force the "Redmond" Windows-like default look-and-feel
  - adds modern desktop-stack integration: plymouth, pipewire-audio,
    xsettingsd, xdg-desktop-portal-trinity, polkitd/polkit-agent-tde,
    tdesudo, network-manager/network-manager-tde, tdebluez-trinity,
    tde-ebook-reader and kdbusnotification-trinity
  - recommends tde-refresh-desktop-base-trinity (Ceratopsian TDE theme)
    instead of the Debian 5/6-era desktop-base-trinity
  - suggests tde-refresh-win9x-trinity (optional Windows 9x themes) and
    tde-refresh-macclassic-trinity and tde-refresh-macosx-trinity (optional
    Mac OS Classic and Mac OS X looks)
 .
 This package intentionally does not depend on the stock tde-trinity or
 redmond-default-settings(-ii)-trinity packages, so it can be installed
 without pulling in their unwanted dependencies.

Package: tde-refresh-desktop-base-trinity
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 desktop-base (>= 13),
 tdebase-trinity,
 tdm-trinity,
 ksplash-trinity,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 plymouth-label
Description: Ceratopsian theme for the Trinity Desktop Environment
 TDE counterpart of Debian's desktop-base: TDE wallpaper, KSplash theme and
 TDM login theme based on the Debian 13 (trixie) Ceratopsian artwork, so TDE
 matches the Plymouth boot splash and the rest of the Debian desktop.
 .
 Unlike desktop-base-trinity (a Debian 5/6-era fork), this package builds on
 the real desktop-base instead of conflicting with and replacing it. It also
 ships the TDE default profile (wallpaper, splash theme) and the kompmgr/
 compton-tde compositor settings.

Package: tde-refresh-win9x-trinity
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 tdebase-trinity,
 tdelibs-trinity,
 tdm-trinity,
 ksplash-trinity,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 gtk2-engines-pixbuf,
 plymouth
Description: Windows 9x look for the Trinity Desktop Environment
 Two ready-to-apply themes for the TDE Theme Manager (Control Center,
 Appearance & Themes):
  - Chicago95: Windows 95 look with the Chicago95 Tux icons, cursors,
    sounds, colour scheme and wallpapers
  - Win9x: the same colour scheme, Redmond window decoration and Windows
    widget style, but keeping TDE's own icons and cursors
 .
 It also installs the Chicago95 GTK2/GTK3/GTK4 themes (with a Metacity
 theme), KSplash and TDM themes, an optional RetroTux Plymouth theme and the
 tde-win9x-panel helper that gives the panel a labelled Start button, and
 tde-win9x-tdm, which gives the classic TDM login screen a Windows look.
 Nothing is activated automatically.
 .
 Artwork comes from the Chicago95 project; TDE settings follow the layout of
 the redmond-default-settings-ii-trinity package, without its dependencies.

Package: tde-refresh-macclassic-trinity
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 tdebase-trinity (>= 4:14.1.7),
 tdelibs-trinity,
 tdeartwork-theme-window-trinity,
 kicker-trinity,
 konqueror-trinity,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Mac OS Classic look for the Trinity Desktop Environment
 Emulates the classic Mac OS interface using TDE's built-in Platinum widget
 style and System++ window decoration, with one bar at the top of the screen
 holding the global menu, applications menu, window list, tray and clock, and
 a Finder-like Konqueror: one icon view per window, each folder in a new window,
 no sidebar or toolbars.
 .
 Nothing is activated on install. The tde-macclassic command applies the whole
 look for the current user and "tde-macclassic revert" restores their previous
 settings. The theme also appears in the TDE Theme Manager, which can set the
 colours, style and decoration only.
 .
 It contains no Apple artwork, logos or fonts.

Package: tde-refresh-macosx-trinity
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 tdebase-trinity (>= 4:14.1.7),
 tdelibs-trinity,
 tde-style-baghira-trinity (>= 4:14.1.7),
 kicker-trinity,
 konqueror-trinity,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Mac OS X look for the Trinity Desktop Environment
 Emulates the Mac OS X interface using the Baghira widget style and window
 decoration, with a bar at the top of the screen holding the global menu,
 Baghira starter, tray and clock, a centred dock-like panel, and a Finder-like
 Konqueror: sidebar, icon view and a compact toolbar, without a location bar.
 .
 Nothing is activated on install. The tde-macosx command applies the whole look
 for the current user and "tde-macosx revert" restores their previous settings.
 The theme also appears in the TDE Theme Manager, which can set the colours,
 style and decoration only.
 .
 It contains no Apple artwork, logos or fonts.
